<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net6.0;net7.0;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Platforms>AnyCPU;x64</Platforms>
    <Description>Micro service architecture using the rabbitmq message broker.</Description>
    <Copyright>Stanislav Batyrgareev</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>BSD-2-Clause</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>http://bsasearch.org/msa.html</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/S-DyX/bsa.msa</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>Git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>MSA Rabbit MQ RabbiMQ RMQ Queue Message Bsa</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>10.0.84
- Builds for .NET 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10.
- Fixed: the consumer dispatcher slept 200 ms or more before every next batch of deliveries (ConsumerWorkService), throughput with prefetchCount 5 grew from ~25 to ~15 000 msg/s.
- Handler workers (degreeOfParallelism &gt; 1) wake up on a signal instead of polling the queue with sleeps up to 1 s.
- Send/Publish overloads with persistent: false send transient messages (delivery mode 1) that the broker does not write to disk.
- RabbitMQ port: "port" in the rabbitMQ section or the connection string, and "host:port" per host; 5672 by default.
- Handler setting internalQueueFormat: "journal" stores the local queue in append-only segment files instead of a file per message; "files" stays the default, old .q files are read in both modes.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <Version>10.0.84</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion></AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion></FileVersion>
    <Authors>Stanislav Batyrgareev</Authors>
    <UserSecretsId>f8fa65d8-3211-4a53-80c0-d6f3de749ad2</UserSecretsId>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>True</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Json" Version="6.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Bsa.Msa.RabbitMq.Core.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
